      "writtenOn": "2022-12-08T15:20:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it important that the `componentType` of an atomic-type is a primitive numeric type? I am wondering if it would be simpler for atomics to just be treated as a fully opaque type, and rely on the existing opaque-type limitations. It could make the implementation a lot simpler and still be correct.\n\nThe GLSL docs define them as such: \"Atomic counters are Opaque Types\" https://www.khronos.org/opengl/wiki/Atomic_Counter\n\nAFAICS the only interaction with an atomic variable is via intrinsic functions, and there\u0027s no direct relation between the `uint` and `atomic_uint` types.",
      "revId": "3d84523969ca71adcd03bf365b12f47693c22352",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5877fb44_d9de0510",
